WEBVTT

0
00:00.140 --> 00:01.610
<v Krista>In this video we're talking about addition</v>

1
00:01.610 --> 00:03.570
and subtraction of mixed numbers.

2
00:03.570 --> 00:05.110
Now remember that a mixed number

3
00:05.110 --> 00:06.960
is a whole number plus a fraction

4
00:06.960 --> 00:10.000
so when I say 2 1/4, that's a mixed number,

5
00:10.000 --> 00:13.900
and it means two plus 1/4 but we write it as 2 1/4.

6
00:13.900 --> 00:16.290
I can also write this as an improper fraction

7
00:16.290 --> 00:19.230
where the numerator is greater than the denominator,

8
00:19.230 --> 00:22.110
but what we wanta do is leave these as mixed numbers

9
00:22.110 --> 00:25.070
and do some addition and subtraction of mixed numbers.

10
00:25.070 --> 00:26.870
So when we're dealing with addition and subtraction

11
00:26.870 --> 00:28.920
of mixed numbers, what we wanta do is add

12
00:28.920 --> 00:30.720
or subtract the whole numbers together,

13
00:30.720 --> 00:33.850
and then separately add or subtract the fractions together,

14
00:33.850 --> 00:35.270
and then combine the two.

15
00:35.270 --> 00:36.593
So when I say 2 1/4 plus 1 1/5,

16
00:37.970 --> 00:40.710
what I wanta do is add the whole numbers together

17
00:40.710 --> 00:42.840
so two and one, so I'll say two plus one.

18
00:42.840 --> 00:44.880
And then separately I wanta add my fractions

19
00:44.880 --> 00:47.010
so I wanta say 1/4 plus 1/5.

20
00:47.010 --> 00:51.403
So plus 1/4 plus 1/5.

21
00:52.540 --> 00:55.220
And now adding my whole numbers is going to be really easy,

22
00:55.220 --> 00:56.810
obviously, that's going to be three.

23
00:56.810 --> 00:58.120
Adding my fractions is going to be

24
00:58.120 --> 00:59.680
a little bit more complicated simply

25
00:59.680 --> 01:02.350
because I'm going to need a common denominator.

26
01:02.350 --> 01:05.480
So what's my common denominator between four and five?

27
01:05.480 --> 01:07.290
Well, if I look for the lowest common multiple

28
01:07.290 --> 01:09.490
using the multiples of five here, I can see

29
01:09.490 --> 01:10.880
that it's going to be 20.

30
01:10.880 --> 01:15.880
And I'm going to haveta multiply 1/4 by five over five

31
01:16.600 --> 01:18.410
to get 20 in the denominator.

32
01:18.410 --> 01:22.920
I'm going to haveta multiply 1/5 by four over four

33
01:22.920 --> 01:24.910
to get 20 in the denominator.

34
01:24.910 --> 01:27.180
So then my result here is going to be two plus one,

35
01:27.180 --> 01:29.660
which is three, and then I'm going to add to that

36
01:29.660 --> 01:33.310
when I do my multiplication here, five times one is five,

37
01:33.310 --> 01:37.710
five times four is 20, four times one is four,

38
01:37.710 --> 01:39.840
four times five is 20.

39
01:39.840 --> 01:42.010
So now I have a common denominator, and I can say

40
01:42.010 --> 01:47.010
that this is three and 5/20 plus 4/20 is nine over 20.

41
01:47.910 --> 01:51.427
So I'm going to get three and nine over 20,

42
01:51.427 --> 01:53.780
and this is going to be my mixed number answer.

43
01:53.780 --> 01:56.320
Now let's look at this example with simple subtraction.

44
01:56.320 --> 02:00.210
I have 11 2/4 minus one and four over six.

45
02:00.210 --> 02:02.950
I can see that both of my fractions can be reduced,

46
02:02.950 --> 02:05.070
2/4 can be reduced to 1/2.

47
02:05.070 --> 02:08.100
Four over six can be reduced to two over three.

48
02:08.100 --> 02:10.090
So I can do the reduction if I wanted to,

49
02:10.090 --> 02:10.970
but I don't have to.

50
02:10.970 --> 02:13.180
I can leave the mixed numbers exactly as they are.

51
02:13.180 --> 02:14.810
So because I have subtraction here,

52
02:14.810 --> 02:18.823
if I pull my whole numbers out, I'm going to get 11 minus one.

53
02:18.823 --> 02:20.350
And then here's the key.

54
02:20.350 --> 02:21.370
Remember, this was addition

55
02:21.370 --> 02:22.950
and we added everything together.

56
02:22.950 --> 02:25.540
When I'm doing subtraction, I can subtract my whole numbers,

57
02:25.540 --> 02:27.730
11 minus one, but then I haveta add

58
02:27.730 --> 02:31.570
to that the subtraction or the difference of my fractions.

59
02:31.570 --> 02:36.480
So I'm going to say plus 2/4 minus four over six.

60
02:36.480 --> 02:39.070
And now here's where I find my common denominator again.

61
02:39.070 --> 02:41.160
The common denominator between four and six

62
02:41.160 --> 02:43.730
is going to be 12, that's the lowest common multiple.

63
02:43.730 --> 02:47.140
So in order to get to 12, I'm going to haveta multiply 2/4

64
02:47.140 --> 02:50.030
by three over three.

65
02:50.030 --> 02:52.350
In order to get to 12 here, I'm going to haveta multiply

66
02:52.350 --> 02:55.420
by two over two so times two over two.

67
02:55.420 --> 02:59.540
And then my result here, 11 minus one is going to give me 10.

68
02:59.540 --> 03:01.670
Then I'm going to add to that my fractions here.

69
03:01.670 --> 03:04.330
So three times two gives me six.

70
03:04.330 --> 03:06.440
Three times four gives me 12.

71
03:06.440 --> 03:10.040
Then subtracted from that, four times two gives me eight.

72
03:10.040 --> 03:14.090
Six times two gives me 12 so I'm going to say 10,

73
03:14.090 --> 03:16.110
and then six minus eight is a negative two

74
03:16.110 --> 03:19.110
so I'm going to get minus two over 12.

75
03:19.110 --> 03:20.970
Now I can't end up with subtraction here

76
03:20.970 --> 03:24.420
as my final step so what I need to do is borrow one

77
03:24.420 --> 03:25.540
from my whole number.

78
03:25.540 --> 03:27.060
Remember here, in this problem we ended up

79
03:27.060 --> 03:29.360
with addition as our final step.

80
03:29.360 --> 03:31.140
We had three plus nine over 20,

81
03:31.140 --> 03:33.060
became three and nine over 20.

82
03:33.060 --> 03:35.350
Here I have subtraction, but I need addition.

83
03:35.350 --> 03:37.600
So what I'm going to do is make this a nine.

84
03:37.600 --> 03:39.110
I'm going to borrow a one from here,

85
03:39.110 --> 03:42.460
and I'm going to add to this 12 over 12.

86
03:42.460 --> 03:45.710
Since I subtracted one here, I had to add one back in,

87
03:45.710 --> 03:48.480
but I wanta go ahead and make the plus one plus 12

88
03:48.480 --> 03:51.360
over 12 so I have a common denominator with my fraction.

89
03:51.360 --> 03:54.690
Now I'm going to have nine and negative two plus 12

90
03:54.690 --> 03:59.170
is a positive 10 so I'm going to have plus 10 over 12.

91
03:59.170 --> 04:01.480
Now I have addition here from my final step,

92
04:01.480 --> 04:03.280
and so I can combine these two and say

93
04:03.280 --> 04:07.000
that this is equal to nine and 10/12.

94
04:07.000 --> 04:08.680
But I can still reduce my fraction.

95
04:08.680 --> 04:11.550
I can divide both numerator and denominator by two

96
04:11.550 --> 04:15.640
so I can actually say that this is nine and five over six.

97
04:15.640 --> 04:18.770
And that's my final answer in a mixed number form.

98
04:18.770 --> 04:21.770
Looking at our final example here, we have 2 3/4

99
04:21.770 --> 04:24.840
plus 3 1/8 plus 7 1/2.

100
04:24.840 --> 04:26.870
So I wanta pull my whole numbers out together.

101
04:26.870 --> 04:30.220
I'm going to get two plus three plus seven

102
04:30.220 --> 04:31.250
for my whole numbers.

103
04:31.250 --> 04:33.810
And then I'm going to say plus my fractions here,

104
04:33.810 --> 04:38.810
3/4 plus 1/8 plus 1/2 for the fractions.

105
04:39.850 --> 04:42.860
I need a common denominator, and the least common multiple

106
04:42.860 --> 04:45.420
of four, eight, and two is eight.

107
04:45.420 --> 04:46.640
Eight is the smallest number

108
04:46.640 --> 04:49.550
that four, eight, and two all divide into evenly.

109
04:49.550 --> 04:51.920
So in order to get eight as a common denominator,

110
04:51.920 --> 04:53.710
I'm going to haveta multiply this first fraction

111
04:53.710 --> 04:55.570
by two over two.

112
04:55.570 --> 04:56.940
This one will stay the same.

113
04:56.940 --> 05:00.290
I'm going to haveta multiply this one by four over four.

114
05:00.290 --> 05:02.580
Now I'll get two plus three is five.

115
05:02.580 --> 05:04.020
Five plus seven is 12.

116
05:04.020 --> 05:07.480
So I'll get 12 plus, multiplying across in the numerator,

117
05:07.480 --> 05:12.480
two times three is six over eight here plus 1/8.

118
05:13.050 --> 05:17.070
Four times one is four so plus four over eight.

119
05:17.070 --> 05:18.960
And now I can add all my fractions together

120
05:18.960 --> 05:22.200
so I get 12 and six plus one is seven.

121
05:22.200 --> 05:23.680
Seven plus four is 11.

122
05:23.680 --> 05:27.120
So I'm going to get 12 plus 11 over eight.

123
05:27.120 --> 05:30.280
Now I could go ahead and write this as 12 11/8,

124
05:30.280 --> 05:31.940
but this is an improper fraction,

125
05:31.940 --> 05:34.380
and I need it to be a proper fraction in order

126
05:34.380 --> 05:36.690
to write my final answer as a mixed number.

127
05:36.690 --> 05:40.920
So I can really say that this is 12 plus eight

128
05:40.920 --> 05:44.240
over eight plus three over eight.

129
05:44.240 --> 05:45.900
Because if I combine these fractions,

130
05:45.900 --> 05:48.540
I would get 11/8, and that's what I had here.

131
05:48.540 --> 05:50.440
So I really just split up this fraction,

132
05:50.440 --> 05:52.653
and the reason I did that is

133
05:52.653 --> 05:53.810
because I have now eight over eight here,

134
05:53.810 --> 05:54.880
which reduces to one.

135
05:54.880 --> 05:57.630
So I just pulled the one out of my fraction,

136
05:57.630 --> 06:01.060
and this becomes 12 plus one

137
06:01.060 --> 06:04.300
plus now a proper fraction three over eight.

138
06:04.300 --> 06:09.240
Twelve plus one is 13 so I get 13 3/8,

139
06:09.240 --> 06:12.230
13 plus 3/8 or 13 3/8,

140
06:12.230 --> 06:15.263
and that's my final answer in mixed number form.